      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "With the increasing numbers of ambulatory surgical patients, anesthetic and post anesthetic care priorities have been identified with the goal of providing safe care and a timely discharge. This article focuses on patient selection, anesthetic options, pain management, nausea and vomiting, and discharge priorities. Collaboration between nursing, anesthesia, and surgical personnel is emphasized throughout."},
